=== Climate ===
Suzuka Prefecture has a humid subtropical climate with a dry-winter variant (Köppen ''Cwa''), characterised by warm temperatures, a pronounced wet season from May through October, and a relatively dry season from November through April. The prefecture's position at the southern tip of Ishijima places it at the transition zone between the tropical monsoon climate of the central Ishijima prefectures and the subtropical climate of [[Yagikoshu]].

The Suzuka Strait creates a distinctive microclimate. The tidal currents through the strait generate sea fog that can persist for days during the spring and autumn transition periods, and the wind funnel effect accelerates coastal breezes to speeds that make the Suzuka coast one of the windiest in Okaiken. The strong winds, combined with the tidal currents, create challenging conditions for maritime navigation but also provide the prefecture with its most important energy resource.

